eq 	ext{true}$ and $!	ext{false} = 	ext{true} 
eq 	ext{false}$ — closed by `cases v <;> simp`; (3) $	ext{Val} = \mathbb{N}$, $f = n+1$: $n+1 
eq n$ by `Nat.succ_ne_self`. Each instance forces the conclusion: no surjection $A 	o (A 	o 	ext{Val})$ can exist for these specific $	ext{Val}$.
